  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1150 AM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nA ridge of high pressure is in control over the Lower Ohio Valley \nallowing for unseasonably warm conditions. Given WAA aloft at \n850 mb and robust mixing in the boundary layer, have bumped up \nhighs a few degrees into the mid 80s today as it is likely temps\nwill continue to overachieve. The NBM has really struggled with\nthe dry air in the column that will also result in much lower \ndewpoints mixing down into the 40s. Minimum relative humidity \nvalues will once again reach 25-30%, with similar values \nexpected across the east Wednesday afternoon. Although there \nwill be an increase in southerly winds due to tighter pressure \ngradient with sfc high pressure building more east, moisture \nrecovery will be slow to occur. Dewpoints eventually return to \nthe 60s and even lower 70s for the latter half of the week. \n\nIn the wake of a cold front on Friday, our warm up will peak on \nWednesday and Thursday with high temperatures near 90 degrees for \nwhat will likely be the final time for this year. NBM continues to \ntrend warmer and is more in line with the GFS/ECMWF with the cold \nfront arriving later. PoPs now peak at a 80-90% chance on \nFriday when the southern stream energy transitions into a \nelongated wave across the FA. Instability remains very meager, \nso we are only looking at transient rumbles of thunder at most.\nThere is a 50-70% chance of showers lingering into Saturday as \nit will not be until Saturday night into Sunday when northern \nstream energy ejects downstream from the Dakotas and pushes the \ndisturbance more eastward. Total rainfall on the NBM continues \nto trend downward with only a 40-50% probability of exceeding \none inch. Due to intervals of light to moderate rain, widespread\nflooding issues are unlikely. \n\nThe weekend into early next week will certainly feel more likely \nfall again as a 1030 mb sfc high pressure over the northern Plains \nushers in much cooler and drier air. High temperatures will trend \ninto the lower 70s with a 20-40% chance of lows dipping into the 40s \nnext Monday morning.",
